    "precision_ceiling_note": "delta_binding_MeV is EXACT (the AME2020 table's own decimal, carried verbatim from ame-2020-binding-energies.witness.json).  Every other number here is NOT: required_rho_over_me_per_link, matches_within_10pct[*].rho_over_me / deviation_pct and link_primitives_MeV_per_unit divide by a SnapPy volume that experimental_constants stores as a float64 literal quoted \u00b11e-12 (VOL_FIGURE_EIGHT_ERR, VOL_THREE_TWIST_ERR; VOL_BORROMEAN_ERR \u00b11e-15), so at most ~12 significant digits are real.  They are serialized as strings only because M_E_MEV is an mpf and this module deliberately does not call _precision.set_compute_dps() \u2014 the mpf arithmetic runs at mpmath's default dps=15, and raising it would print the volume's binary tail out to output_dps rather than add information.  Read these as float64-grade values in string form; do NOT quote them past ~12 digits, and do NOT read their string type as evidence of precision.  Closing this properly needs exact high-precision sources for Vol(4_1) and Vol(5_2), as VOL_BORROMEAN_50DPS_STR already is.",
